       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 4,250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (some references allow 3,000 mg/day). The most per single dose is typically 1,000 mg, or 850 mg in some labeling.\n- **Risk:** This dose is about 5 times the maximum. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **425 mg** PO three times daily, which isn't a standard tablet strength\n- **1,000 mg** PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 4,250 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest talking with pharmacy first."
      }
